A||||4||Seanh||Stupid Valve question||||5||
Z||000000||Seanh||11-09-2000||09:04 PM||||I was just thinking about this before I start on my 85. I took the heads off my 86 and put them back on, and had to adjust the valve lash. If I were to make a mark on the rods as to their position to the guides, could I get away with not doing the valve lash adjusting? Just wondering because that would make it a little easier. I, being the stupid person I am, started adjusting the valve lash and then noticed I didnt put the distributor back in. I dont know what good it did my to mark its position before removing it since I didnt put it in before moving the engine.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">    <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||11-09-2000||09:50 PM||||Nope, that procedure won't work!<P>If you followed the book when doing your valve lash and started with # 1 TDC, rotated the crank 1 revolution and stopped, you should be at #4's firing position. If you can visualize the rotor pointing at #1 cylinder, insert the distributor 180 degrees off of that (kind of pointing at the gap between the air cleaner and the bulkhead). This should be  in the correct position.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||11-09-2000||10:12 PM||||Darn, oh well. One more question then. I was going to time the engine last night and I couldnt for the life of me see the timing marks worth crap. What is the best angle to see the marks? I have more trouble with a timeing light and all. Also, when I turned the engine on my 86 I had the belts off, can it be done with them on? Thanks<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seanhsig.gif">    <BR>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||11-10-2000||02:44 AM||||Well, the wider of the 3 slots is the one you want to use to time with. What I do is to turn the crank to where I can get to it with a tooth pick or model paint brush and lay in some white paint.<P>You should be able to turn the engine with the belts on. I jack them up and use a breaker bar on the balancer bolt, much easier to get to (best to mark the balancer too!).<BR> <BR>When seting the timing look down from the top of the strut tower and behind the water pump pulley to view the crankshaft balancer.<P> You have the procedure, right?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||11-10-2000||07:52 AM||||Okay, Thanks. Yes, I have the timing procedure. I will try painting it tonight, might help alot. I have the right rear wheel on right now, but just because I am working on the engine. I have the splash guard off, and I will take the tire off tonight. Thanks||||reg||1
